From: PowOS <noreply@powback.com>
Subject: [PATCH] folder view: on the desktop, a finger swiped up on the background opens the app launcher

A phone's app drawer: a touch drag mostly upward on the desktop's empty background (where it would start a rubber
band selection) opens the application launcher. Here, not in the compositor: to KWin the desktop is one surface, so
its swipe filter also fired when moving or resizing a widget upward (kwin patch 0009 now does panels only). A mouse
still selects.
---
--- a/containments/desktop/package/contents/ui/FolderView.qml
+++ b/containments/desktop/package/contents/ui/FolderView.qml
@@ -529,6 +529,17 @@
                     dragY = -1;
                     clearPressState();
                 } else {
+                    // PowOS: on the desktop a finger swiped up on the empty background opens the app launcher (a phone's
+                    // app drawer) instead of selecting - here, where it can tell the background from a widget (to the
+                    // compositor the desktop is one surface: moving or resizing a widget upward opened it too). A mouse
+                    // still selects.
+                    if (main.isRootView && !root.isPopup && mouse.source === Qt.MouseEventSynthesizedByQt
+                            && pressY - mouse.y > Math.abs(mouse.x - pressX)) {
+                        clearPressState();
+                        Plasmoid.containment.corona.activateLauncherMenu();
+                        return;
+                    }
+
                     // Disable rubberband in popup list view mode or while renaming
                     if (root.useListViewMode || (main.editor && main.editor.targetItem) || (verticalScrollBar.active || horizontalScrollBar.active)) {
                         return;
